---
title: "10e  Revenue administration beyond collecting tax"
---
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: What precedes and follows collection and how does it enter Treasury and accounting?
  %% SOURCES: [PEFA2025] [PD1445] BIR / BOC rules require case-specific verification
  %% SCOPE: Reference view; not a verified deployed system interface.
  %% READING: Arrows show possible evidence, authority or event dependencies, not a universal time order or verified API.
flowchart TB
  LAW["Tax / fee law and implementing regulation"] --> BASE["Register taxpayers / taxable bases / obligations"]
  BASE --> FILE["Declare, assess or determine amount due"]
  FILE --> DUE["Receivable / assessed obligation when legally applicable"]
  DUE --> PAY{"Paid by due date?"}
  PAY -->|Yes| COL["Collect through approved channel"]
  PAY -->|No| AR["Record arrears / assess penalties / enforce or litigate as permitted"]
  AR --> COL
  COL --> BANK["Agent bank / collection gateway / Treasury receipt"]
  BANK --> TSA["Remit / settle to BTr treasury accounts"]
  COL --> TAXREC["BIR / BOC / agency collection record"]
  TSA --> TREAS["BTr cash and government books"]
  TAXREC --> REC["Match declaration, bank report, government record"]
  TREAS --> REC
  REC --> REF["Refund, offset, adjustment, disputed assessment when applicable"]
  REC --> AUDIT["Revenue reporting and audit"]
